WEBVTT

00:00:14.217 --> 00:00:17.345
You aren't to blame for Will's death.

00:00:19.055 --> 00:00:22.459
Do you know something?

00:00:22.459 --> 00:00:24.894
I do.

00:00:24.894 --> 00:00:27.530
Please tell me.

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:31.468
His... Will's...

00:00:31.468 --> 00:00:33.402
...time had come.

00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:49.611
You still had Solty!

00:00:53.556 --> 00:00:54.716
That hurt...

00:00:56.459 --> 00:01:04.134
Nee ima made shiritakatta
otogi-banashi no tsuzuki

00:01:04.134 --> 00:01:10.698
Eien ni owaranai
shiawase nara kono te de

00:01:12.308 --> 00:01:22.285
Bokura wa marude
ichimai-chigai no guuzen o sagashiatte

00:01:22.285 --> 00:01:24.454
Meguriatta

00:01:24.454 --> 00:01:32.629
Kimi ga itsuka nomikonda sono kotoba yori

00:01:32.629 --> 00:01:41.538
Zutto iezu ni itekureteta yasashisa o

00:01:41.538 --> 00:01:48.511
Shinjitai to ima omounda

00:01:48.511 --> 00:01:56.252
Nee kono saki wa doko made
mo fuan to tonari-awase

00:01:56.252 --> 00:02:02.592
Nakusu mono ga nakatta
bokutachi wa mou inai

00:02:02.592 --> 00:02:10.300
Nee ima made shiranakatta
otogi-banashi no tsuzuki

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:16.639
Eien ni owaranai
shiawase nara kono te de

00:02:16.639 --> 00:02:20.473
Tsumikasanete yuku mono

00:02:27.283 --> 00:02:29.452
"I Was Half Kidding"

00:02:29.452 --> 00:02:31.921
"I Was Half Kidding"
His parents abandoned him
when he was just a young boy.

00:02:31.921 --> 00:02:34.354
His parents abandoned him
when he was just a young boy.

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:36.356
By the time he realized what had happened,

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:39.660
he found himself wandering
the city streets alone.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.926
Then came the horrific Blast Fall.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.791
He teetered on the brink of life and death.

00:03:10.791 --> 00:03:13.961
What saved him then
was resemble technology,

00:03:13.961 --> 00:03:18.599
which was still in its nascent stages.

00:03:18.599 --> 00:03:21.802
But his physician was a corrupt man.

00:03:21.802 --> 00:03:25.005
His objective was the victim subsidies
paid out by the city

00:03:25.005 --> 00:03:28.141
and the operations
he performed were slipshod.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:32.446
With inferior resemble parts
and insufficient post-operative care,

00:03:32.446 --> 00:03:36.283
Will's body began to
deteriorate from the inside.

00:03:36.283 --> 00:03:39.887
By the time anyone realized what
had happened, it was already too late.

00:03:39.887 --> 00:03:43.090
Did you know that?

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:47.027
Both you... and Mr. Will?

00:03:47.027 --> 00:03:48.228
We knew.

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.930
Then, why?

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.966
I am an idle spectator,
who gave up the world.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:56.069
I will not interfere,
no matter what others might do.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.939
But that is no reason to...

00:03:58.939 --> 00:04:03.243
Will wandered here and
decided on his own to stay.

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:08.078
He probably found it comfortable
precisely because I didn't meddle.

00:04:09.917 --> 00:04:13.854
There is something Will said to me one day.

00:04:13.854 --> 00:04:16.456
Did you know, Gramps?

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:20.127
A luminous snow falls on that city.

00:04:20.127 --> 00:04:21.795
A luminous snow?

00:04:21.795 --> 00:04:22.863
Yeah.

00:04:22.863 --> 00:04:27.434
That's right, and I still remember it.

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:32.272
I despise the Blast Fall
for what it did to my body,

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:36.910
but at that moment,
there definitely was a luminous snowfall.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:40.547
It was so beautiful and so ethereal.

00:04:40.547 --> 00:04:46.119
In a corner of my mind, I knew
something terrible had happened,

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:49.957
but I couldn't look away.

00:04:49.957 --> 00:04:54.528
Don't tell me you're building
a plane to see that?

00:04:54.528 --> 00:04:59.032
No. I'd die before I ever got to see it.

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:01.735
Then, why?

00:05:01.735 --> 00:05:03.003
It's just...

00:05:03.003 --> 00:05:07.708
Maybe it's just that I want to believe.

00:05:07.708 --> 00:05:11.044
Like when I saw that luminous snow.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:15.003
That this world is a beautiful place.

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:19.152
I am an idle spectator.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:22.689
I will not interfere,
no matter what others might do.

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:25.192
Even whatever it is that you do after this,

00:05:25.192 --> 00:05:27.490
I will do nothing but watch.

00:05:42.609 --> 00:05:45.912
Feeling refreshed now that you've
washed your face after all that time?

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.347
Yeah.

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:50.350
Your punch yesterday really stung.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:53.842
Oh? It hurt me, too.

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:57.491
It brought back memories.

00:05:57.491 --> 00:05:59.326
How many years has it been?

00:05:59.326 --> 00:06:01.995
Not since the year you became a hunter.

00:06:01.995 --> 00:06:05.132
Is that right? Has it been that long?

00:06:05.132 --> 00:06:08.135
It stung back then, too.

00:06:08.135 --> 00:06:09.770
Have you made up your mind?

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.796
Yeah, I've come to my senses.

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:30.624
So, they still haven't found her.

00:06:30.624 --> 00:06:33.560
What're you looking so intently at?

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:36.129
A missing persons bulletin board?

00:06:36.129 --> 00:06:39.499
I didn't know you were still
searching for your parents.

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:43.637
Hey! What're you two doing? Let's go.

00:06:43.637 --> 00:06:44.538
Coming.

00:06:44.538 --> 00:06:45.605
Right!

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:47.507
Well, not that there's
anything wrong with it.

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:50.477
I won't tell those two about it.

00:06:50.477 --> 00:06:53.914
Thank you. I'd appreciate that.

00:06:53.914 --> 00:06:56.116
But in exchange, dinner is on you tonight.

00:06:56.116 --> 00:06:57.617
Okay, it's settled!

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:58.743
What?

00:07:04.491 --> 00:07:05.958
Where did she go?

00:07:14.134 --> 00:07:16.470
You're going to repair the plane?

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:17.604
Yes.

00:07:17.604 --> 00:07:19.406
What for?

00:07:19.406 --> 00:07:22.776
An homage to Will?

00:07:22.776 --> 00:07:24.077
I do not know.

00:07:24.077 --> 00:07:27.478
It is just something that
I feel I want to do, so...

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:33.520
That's the mainframe
that supports everything.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:35.055
If you change its shape haphazardly,

00:07:35.055 --> 00:07:38.291
it will buckle easily
and won't be able to bear the load.

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:39.359
What?

00:07:39.359 --> 00:07:44.297
For a plane to fly, it must
have both lift and thrust

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:47.630
to overcome gravity and drag.

00:07:49.603 --> 00:07:52.572
In order to withstand those heavy loads,

00:07:52.572 --> 00:07:56.409
it must have a precisely calculated
structure and light weight.

00:07:56.409 --> 00:07:59.746
Huh? Uh...

00:07:59.746 --> 00:08:04.351
Will's schematics should
be on his workbench.

00:08:04.351 --> 00:08:08.989
You'll be better off working with those,
rather than working from scratch.

00:08:08.989 --> 00:08:11.558
Thank you very much.

00:08:11.558 --> 00:08:13.992
Just an old man's ramblings.

00:08:25.639 --> 00:08:29.843
People have things in their past
that they would rather not remember.

00:08:29.843 --> 00:08:33.813
We shoulder such sinful pasts,

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:36.179
you and I.

00:08:37.984 --> 00:08:41.421
Are you seriously planning
to do such a thing?!

00:08:41.421 --> 00:08:45.725
Spit at the heavens and it is certain
to come back down upon you!

00:08:45.725 --> 00:08:47.625
And you would still insist?

00:08:49.162 --> 00:08:51.460
I suppose it's no use trying to stop you.

00:08:54.401 --> 00:09:00.040
After that, I left your side
and became an idle spectator.

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:05.812
But I am sure your ambitions
have yet to crumble,

00:09:05.812 --> 00:09:07.336
Ashley.

00:09:08.582 --> 00:09:10.584
Division Chief.

00:09:10.584 --> 00:09:14.154
Regarding the clock tower incident
the other day...

00:09:14.154 --> 00:09:18.825
As expected, the suspect
is definitely Jeremy Kolbel.

00:09:18.825 --> 00:09:19.960
The extent of the damage,

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.562
compared to the electrical potential
of the Aurora Wave was approximately...

00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:25.065
Spare me the detailed figures.

00:09:25.065 --> 00:09:27.734
I'll leave the rest to all of you.

00:09:27.734 --> 00:09:31.705
Once everything is taken care of,
submit your report.

00:09:31.705 --> 00:09:33.104
That is all.

00:09:38.211 --> 00:09:41.214
How did it go?

00:09:41.214 --> 00:09:45.913
Just as I thought, she's superior
in every measurable way to Accela.

00:09:47.654 --> 00:09:49.656
I have had to wait so long.

00:09:49.656 --> 00:09:54.525
It seems I'll finally be able
to break free of your curse.

00:10:04.104 --> 00:10:05.772
You know, Silvia...

00:10:05.772 --> 00:10:07.340
Huh? What is it?

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:08.642
What? What?

00:10:08.642 --> 00:10:10.844
You work on that report!

00:10:10.844 --> 00:10:12.412
Okay.

00:10:12.412 --> 00:10:15.815
Don't you think the division chief
was acting strangely earlier?

00:10:15.815 --> 00:10:18.351
Strangely? How?

00:10:18.351 --> 00:10:21.154
I can't quite put a finger on it, but...

00:10:21.154 --> 00:10:23.657
Nothing really seemed out of the ordinary.

00:10:23.657 --> 00:10:27.994
Though, he did seem a little busy
and came across kind of brusque.

00:10:27.994 --> 00:10:32.265
Brusque! Brusque! Brusque!

00:10:32.265 --> 00:10:33.466
Did you feel a little hurt?!

00:10:33.466 --> 00:10:35.602
You just keep working!

00:10:35.602 --> 00:10:38.271
Okay...

00:10:38.271 --> 00:10:39.973
Doesn't it bother you?

00:10:39.973 --> 00:10:41.574
Not really.

00:10:41.574 --> 00:10:45.203
As long as I get paid,
I don't care either way.

00:11:11.638 --> 00:11:13.306
You guys...

00:11:13.306 --> 00:11:17.744
Here, it's what we've put together
so far on Solty's whereabouts.

00:11:17.744 --> 00:11:20.080
Thanks, Miranda.

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:22.982
You can thank me when you get back.

00:11:22.982 --> 00:11:25.719
You're going to go
looking for Solty, right?

00:11:25.719 --> 00:11:28.254
- Then take me with you...
- I'm going alone.

00:11:28.254 --> 00:11:29.122
But...

00:11:29.122 --> 00:11:33.727
Sorry. I have to go alone.

00:11:33.727 --> 00:11:35.662
Then get going!

00:11:35.662 --> 00:11:38.465
- Kash...
- Hurry up and find Solty!

00:11:38.465 --> 00:11:40.166
Come on, quickly!

00:11:40.166 --> 00:11:43.937
Okay, I'm on my way.

00:11:43.937 --> 00:11:46.701
You're too slow, stupid.

00:11:49.909 --> 00:11:53.546
Thank goodness. It is not
as broken as I had thought.

00:11:53.546 --> 00:11:56.276
Even I should be able to fix this.

00:13:56.603 --> 00:14:02.909
Lines 42, 44, and 48 through 66
have been severed.

00:14:02.909 --> 00:14:05.645
Blood pressure and respiration
are both rising!

00:14:05.645 --> 00:14:09.182
Tension coefficient rising rapidly.
We're seeing signs of rejection.

00:14:09.182 --> 00:14:10.450
Pupils dilating.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.552
Control speed decreasing.

00:14:12.552 --> 00:14:16.289
As expected, this appears to be her limit.

00:14:16.289 --> 00:14:17.756
That settles it, then.

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:34.574
Well? Isn't this view the best you've seen?

00:14:34.574 --> 00:14:36.735
Yes! It is the best!

00:14:46.052 --> 00:14:48.821
Maybe it's just that I want to believe.

00:14:48.821 --> 00:14:52.018
That this world is a beautiful place.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:04.404
Oh, I'm Will. Nice to meet you.

00:15:04.404 --> 00:15:06.573
But if you have any lingering attachments,

00:15:06.573 --> 00:15:08.841
why not try clinging to them for now?

00:15:08.841 --> 00:15:11.644
No matter how shameless it may seem.

00:15:11.644 --> 00:15:13.913
You can always throw them away later.

00:15:13.913 --> 00:15:15.210
At any time.

00:15:17.417 --> 00:15:19.385
Can't you tell?

00:15:19.385 --> 00:15:21.979
- That I'm in love with you!
- Huh?!

00:15:25.625 --> 00:15:28.719
I was half serious.

00:15:31.297 --> 00:15:34.596
Rise up!

00:16:07.033 --> 00:16:11.094
Have you decided what it is
that you want to do?

00:16:12.605 --> 00:16:14.232
Have you decided?

00:16:16.242 --> 00:16:20.702
You know, I loved you, Mr. Will.

00:16:23.883 --> 00:16:26.852
I am half kidding.

00:16:27.854 --> 00:16:32.825
You knew about the state
of your own health...

00:16:32.825 --> 00:16:35.228
Was it not painful?

00:16:35.228 --> 00:16:36.729
Did it not hurt?

00:16:36.729 --> 00:16:40.199
- I threw it all away.
- What?

00:16:40.199 --> 00:16:46.305
The pain, the hurt...
I threw away all such feelings.

00:16:46.305 --> 00:16:48.608
Why? How?

00:16:48.608 --> 00:16:52.311
Because I realized I had
become unable to laugh.

00:16:52.311 --> 00:16:56.916
If I was going to live anyway,
I wanted to live a life with laughter.

00:16:56.916 --> 00:16:59.385
You are very strong.

00:16:59.385 --> 00:17:02.877
But I cannot laugh.

00:17:04.657 --> 00:17:07.794
What could a mechanical puppet
like you understand?!

00:17:07.794 --> 00:17:10.196
I cannot laugh yet.

00:17:10.196 --> 00:17:13.766
You just have to throw it all away,
that's all.

00:17:13.766 --> 00:17:16.436
Whether it's family or friends...

00:17:16.436 --> 00:17:19.098
Love or life...

00:17:19.939 --> 00:17:23.943
You just have to throw away
everything you have.

00:17:23.943 --> 00:17:25.845
But if...

00:17:25.845 --> 00:17:29.882
But if you have any lingering attachments,

00:17:29.882 --> 00:17:32.618
why not try clinging to them for now?

00:17:32.618 --> 00:17:35.521
You can always throw them away later.

00:17:35.521 --> 00:17:37.148
At any time.

00:17:38.891 --> 00:17:42.224
You are mean, Mr. Will.

00:17:45.064 --> 00:17:48.735
Will I be able to laugh again?

00:17:48.735 --> 00:17:53.900
With this body... again?

00:18:35.214 --> 00:18:38.117
Seems you had a safe flight.

00:18:38.117 --> 00:18:39.152
Yes.

00:18:39.152 --> 00:18:40.920
Congratulations.

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:44.323
I'm sure Will is happy, too.

00:18:44.323 --> 00:18:47.527
There is something I would like to ask you.

00:18:47.527 --> 00:18:48.795
What is it?

00:18:48.795 --> 00:18:52.031
It is about something Mr. Will said to me.

00:18:52.031 --> 00:18:56.402
He said he wanted to leave
his own little mark on this world.

00:18:56.402 --> 00:19:00.406
What do you think he meant by that?

00:19:00.406 --> 00:19:05.311
Probably that he wanted
someone to remember him.

00:19:05.311 --> 00:19:11.484
He wanted to engrave proof
of his life in someone's memory.

00:19:11.484 --> 00:19:13.920
That was a cruel thing Will did...

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:20.526
I will never forget
about Mr. Will. Not ever.

00:19:20.526 --> 00:19:21.694
I see.

00:19:21.694 --> 00:19:23.429
I will never throw away...

00:19:23.429 --> 00:19:27.266
...my memories of Mr. Will,
or what has happened up until now.

00:19:27.266 --> 00:19:30.803
I will take them all with me.

00:19:30.803 --> 00:19:35.141
I am an idle spectator. I won't meddle.

00:19:35.141 --> 00:19:37.541
Not even to ask you where you're headed.

00:19:39.111 --> 00:19:41.375
Thank you for everything.

00:19:52.658 --> 00:19:54.927
Times change...

00:19:54.927 --> 00:19:57.396
For better, or for worse,

00:19:57.396 --> 00:20:01.234
the only one who clings to the past
without trying to change it is...

00:20:01.234 --> 00:20:03.498
...an old man's obsession.

00:20:08.574 --> 00:20:11.644
The division chief certainly is late.

00:20:11.644 --> 00:20:16.482
I wonder just what he wants,
calling us together after work...

00:20:16.482 --> 00:20:18.851
Integra, do you know what this is about?

00:20:18.851 --> 00:20:21.354
No, I have no idea.

00:20:21.354 --> 00:20:24.290
I don't really care about all that,

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:27.426
but we better be getting
paid overtime for this!

00:20:27.426 --> 00:20:28.527
You be quiet.

00:20:28.527 --> 00:20:30.859
It's a reasonable expectation!

00:20:32.798 --> 00:20:36.996
Hello. I'm sorry for being late.

00:20:39.205 --> 00:20:40.139
Not at all.

00:20:40.139 --> 00:20:44.510
Now, what I've come to tell you
is none other than this.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:50.816
Do you know my selection standards
for choosing my subordinates?

00:20:50.816 --> 00:20:51.951
Because they're your type!

00:20:51.951 --> 00:20:53.386
Celica!

00:20:53.386 --> 00:20:57.056
I like superior individuals.

00:20:57.056 --> 00:21:01.494
Gender, age, education, birth...

00:21:01.494 --> 00:21:04.430
Such things have nothing to do with it.

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:07.199
You are superior individuals

00:21:07.199 --> 00:21:10.503
and that is why I selected you
to work for me.

00:21:10.503 --> 00:21:14.807
It follows then, that if someone
more superior should appear,

00:21:14.807 --> 00:21:18.878
I would place that person over you.

00:21:18.878 --> 00:21:20.479
What?

00:21:20.479 --> 00:21:22.413
Now, let me introduce you.

00:21:26.185 --> 00:21:29.455
This is your new superior as of today.

00:21:29.455 --> 00:21:31.548
Rose Anderson.

00:21:52.642 --> 00:21:57.413
Hareta hi no kouen

00:21:57.413 --> 00:22:00.349
Miageta sora ni

00:22:00.349 --> 00:22:08.950
Kiesou ni natta chiisana Little Cloud

00:22:11.594 --> 00:22:16.365
Kaze ni mi o makasete

00:22:16.365 --> 00:22:19.302
Jiyuu ni ikiru

00:22:19.302 --> 00:22:25.298
Sukoshi-zutsu aruku watashi-tachi

00:22:27.343 --> 00:22:30.107
Onnaji dane

00:22:32.114 --> 00:22:36.886
Taisetsu na jikan

00:22:36.886 --> 00:22:40.723
Deau tabi ni

00:22:40.723 --> 00:22:50.266
Hitori ja nai kono kimochi
yasashisa ni naru

00:22:50.266 --> 00:22:56.839
Dareka o shinjiru yuuki ni kaete

00:22:56.839 --> 00:23:09.309
Kitto kono mama
ano sora no hate ni kieru mae ni

00:23:15.624 --> 00:23:18.227
I won't acknowledge you!

00:23:18.227 --> 00:23:19.729
Silvia!

00:23:19.729 --> 00:23:22.231
Next time, "Lady".

00:23:22.231 --> 00:23:25.928
Girls become beautiful
when they fall in love.
